Earth's relief (ETOPO5) on 163842 cells; valley floors at the lowest 0.1 of each cell's land points
the ocean of the data holds 1.33758e+18 m3 of water below 0 m; the planet file has 1.33500e+18 m3, 0.19 % less. Poured here: the first; the sea of the mesh comes to rest at +1.9 m and covers 70.75 % of the planet, with 47962 land cells

1. How coarse the heights are, and how often they tie
every height of the data is a whole number of metres: yes; of its land (by area), 48 % lies within half a metre of a whole number of hundreds of feet
on the mesh, of 47962 land cells 16510 (34.4 %) have a land neighbour at exactly their own height; the commonest heights handed to Drainage: 91 m (1627 cells), 61 m (1392 cells), 30 m (1327 cells), 152 m (1246 cells), 122 m (1129 cells)
of 42657 land cells with a lower neighbour, 9641 (22.6 %) have several equally low: the lower bed settles 3341, the wider way 6249, the cell numbers 51; another 4578 land cells (9.5 %) lie on level ground
with every hollow full, the water of 0.04 % of the land's area reaches the sea in another cell when the order of the cells is turned round, and of 14.9 % when the wider way is left out and the cell numbers settle the ties

2. The closed hollows of the data on their own grid, and of the mesh
the data: the ocean (water below 0 m joined to the open Pacific) covers 71.1 % of the planet. Of all that is not ocean, 13.3 % lies under water when every hollow of the data is full (14.8 % between 60 south and 60 north); of the land above 0 m alone, 12.6 % (13.9 %)
the mesh: 29.3 % of the planet is not sea. Of it, 10.5 % lies under water when every hollow is full (11.9 % between 60 south and 60 north); 62.4 % drains into a closed hollow

